plugin-qualify (0.20.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.20.1
  * tests: an LV2 cell holds latencyMs beside its latency
  * judged-layer: cite plugin-db's records design note by its public issue
  * fixtures: the Pi records are named for the plugin-qualify that wrote
    them, not a date
  * judged-layer: the command that prints a record's plugin-db layer, or why
    it has none
  * judged layer: a record converted to plugin-db's judged layer; the latency
    line and the rules declared once
  * isolated step: a conditional reason beside the memory gap owes it too
  * records-package: one package per cell of a run
  * footprint: the record states the notes held (voices) the figure was
    measured at (#316)
  * sync: a distributed set applies only at the cell it was measured at
  * lv2-measure: a cost and latency run takes each plugin's pin (#316)
  * isolated pass: a plugin with no pin is pinned once its step has run (#316)
  * record: a cell not attempted is labelled not-attempted, not probe-error
    (#316)
  * host class: x86_64 from uname -m is x86-64 (#316)
  * refreshPins says why a pin was not refreshed (#316)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:48:29 +0000
